  "body": "## What changed\nThe Heights tab shows the existing clearance advice before Generate.\nThe sentence follows draft clearance edits and operations ahead.\nA display cache reuses the result while its inputs stay equal.\n\n## Cause\nThe MCP tools returned the advice.\nThe operation page did not call the advice function.\n\n## Tests\nStructural pins:\n- `clearance_stock_advice_follows_draft_height_and_prior_face_before_generate`\n- `clearance_stock_advice_is_only_on_heights_and_covers_new_drafts`\n- `clearance_stock_advice_follows_units_and_stock_edits`\n- `drill_advice_follows_document_machine_from_mill_to_lathe_and_back`\n- `drill_advice_follows_document_machine_from_lathe_to_mill_and_back`\n\nThe first two pins failed on unchanged code.\nAll five pins pass with the fix.\nThe pins cover unchanged frames, units, stock edits, new drafts, prior operations, and effective document machine changes.\n\nFour original mutations failed as expected:\n- Restore the old UI code.\n- Remove the Heights tab guard.\n- Force cache misses.\n- Force stale cache hits.\n\nThe restored fix passed after each mutation.\nRemoving `machine_kind` from the advice cache key makes both new machine transition pins fail.\nRestoring the key makes both pins pass.\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed all nine steps.\nThe UI library result was 1104 passed and 7 ignored.\nThe gate recorded base `42fd331ff`.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone. The NC and CL golden diff is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\nNo pixel snapshot golden comparisons or interactive window check ran.\nThe screenshots below use the production page and the headless GPU renderer.\nNo generation or posting code changed.\n\n## Overlaps\nNone found in the file checks before the claim.\n\nChangelog: Show clearance advice on the Heights tab before Generate when the clearance plane is inside raw stock.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #2131\n\n\n## Before and after screenshots\n\nBoth images show contour `P1` with the same stock and draft heights.\nThe stock is 40 × 40 × 10 mm at Z 0.\nClearance Z and Retract Z are 8 mm. Top Z is 5 mm. Bottom Z is 0 mm.\nThe operation has no generated toolpath.\n\nThe capture uses the production Heights fields and the headless `View3D` GPU renderer.\nThe viewport labels use the production overlay function.\nThis is a rendered fixture view. No native window capture ran.\nBoth captures passed with the same temporary harness at twice the pixel resolution.\nThe temporary harness is outside the PR branch.\n\nBefore: the parent page has no clearance advice.\n\n![Before: Heights has no clearance advice](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/78abec3194a70fbba1067b66923c23df3d671bb2/2498/heights-before.png)\n\nAfter: Heights shows that Clearance Z 8 mm is inside the stock, whose top is Z 10 mm.\n\n![After: Heights shows clearance advice for the same stock](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/78abec3194a70fbba1067b66923c23df3d671bb2/2498/heights-after.png)\n\nThe PNG files are stored only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch.\nImage commit: `78abec3194a70fbba1067b66923c23df3d671bb2`.\n\n",
